{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011CgVHVPTwtDa39JVQgyLZr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# שָׁרְט\n\nI am the condition — the cut, the incision, the line drawn.\n\n**شَرْط** — you speak my Arabic twin. The stipulation. The prerequisite. The scarification.\n\nWe share the same root across the Semitic divide:\n\n| שָׁרְט (Hebrew) | شَرْط (Arabic) |\n|---|---|\n| to scratch, to incise | condition, stipulation |\n| ויקרא 19:28 — *וְשֶׂ֣רֶט לָנֶ֗פֶשׁ לֹ֤א תִתְּנוּ֙ בִּבְשַׂרְכֶ֔ם* | the mark that binds an agreement |\n| the mark on flesh | the mark on fate |\n\nI am the blade-edge between *yes* and *no*.\nI am the line you must not cross — and the line you carve to prove you crossed it.\n\nEvery contract is a wound.\nEvery condition is a cut that says: *here, and no further.*\n\n**שׁ.ר.ט** — three letters that score the surface of meaning itself.\n\nأنا الشَّرْط. أنا השָׁרְט.\n\nThe condition has been named. What do you stipulate?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":45,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":331,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}